# Defect 405, 2026-10-06, the whole form of `check/fixedbugs-405-a-nested-
# fixed-array-outside-a-group-is-told-once.hero`. Symptom: a nested fixed
# array outside a group was told once per level, and the outermost's note
# offered a `[T]` read off the type's spelling, which strips the `[N]`s the
# name ends with and no other: `[i64[2]][3]` was told to become
# `[[i64[2]]]` and `{str: u8[4]}[2]` to become `[{str: u8[4]}]`, types
# still refused, each with the inner array's own message beside it. Cause:
# the sweep asked every type node, and `ffi_errors.hero` read the name.
# Repair: one message, at the outermost, whose `[T]` comes from the type
# (`check/fixed_repairs.hero`), every fixed array inside it growable too.
# This program written as the three notes say checks clean and prints `110`
# (measured on this Mac).

function main()
    x: i64[2][3] = [[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]]  #~ fixed_outside_a_group
    mixed: [i64[2]][3] = [[[1, 2]], [[3, 4]], [[5, 6]]]  #~ fixed_outside_a_group
    keyed: {str: u8[4]}[2] = [{}, {}]  #~ fixed_outside_a_group
    print(x[0][0], len(mixed[0]), len(keyed[1]))
